# GitHub OAuth app client id, used for the device-flow sign-in.
#
# You only need this when running from source. Released builds have Chief's own
# client id compiled in, so people who install the app configure nothing.
#
# There is no client secret: Chief uses GitHub's device flow precisely so that
# no secret has to ship inside the binary, and a client id is not sensitive —
# it is visible in every OAuth flow. That is why the release workflow reads it
# from a repository *variable* rather than a secret.
#
# To use your own for development: GitHub → Settings → Developer settings →
# OAuth Apps → New OAuth App, then enable "Device flow" on the app's page.
CHIEF_GITHUB_CLIENT_ID=
